        {% for item in items %}
            &lt;div class=&quot;item&quot;&gt;
                &lt;a href=&quot;{{ item.get_absolute_url }}&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;img src=&quot;{% if item.image %}{{ item.image.url }}{% else %}{% static &quot;img/no_image.png&quot; %}{% endif %}&quot;&gt;
                &lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;a href=&quot;{{ item.get_absolute_url }}&quot;&gt;{{ item.name }}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
                ${{ item.price }}
            &lt;/div&gt;
        {% endfor %}
    &lt;/div&gt;
{% endblock %}
</code></pre>
<p>I thought that it was because of catalog.html, which includes the navbar and title, so i commented it out. But now it shows nothing</p>,"<p>you are not sending 'items' in context of itemListView function. you should use code something like this:</p>

