However, once I close one of the connections (ctrl+c) they BOTH close.
In the end, only the data from the manually closed connection is received. The other one, from a separate <code>nc</code> on a separate ssh server never reaches the <code>client.on(&quot;close&quot;)</code> part, it seems. It's just terminated for no reason.</p>
<p>Any ideas? I don't even know where to start.</p>
<p>//EDIT
Just tested it from my pc and some ssh mobile app using separated SSH servers. As soon as ctrl+c is sent at any device it closes the connection for all clients.</p>
