</code></pre>
<p>Specifically, whenever I enter a &quot;$&quot; sign into the form, my code will remove the &quot;$&quot; sign and validate the input as usual. However, when the input is invalid, it no longer highlights the input box in yellow.</p>
<p>May I know what is going on and how can this be fixed using vanilla javascript? Thank you</p>,"<p>Your issue is that you're adding the yellow highlight, but then removing it in your final for loop, this is due to your final for loop using <code>price_len</code>, which is calculated <em>before</em> you remove the <code>$</code>. As a result, your for loop is doing one additional iteration, and so <code>.charAt(i)</code> tries to access an index not in your string giving you an empty string. To fix this, you can calculate the length after you've removed the additional <code>$</code>:</p>

